\subsection{Method 0: Centralised Per-Second Phase Controller}
\label{sec:sol_centralised}
% ----------------------------------------------------

The centralised controller operates at a fixed 1\,Hz cadence, bypassing
bus-triggered detection entirely.  At each second, all 12 intersections are
evaluated simultaneously using Kalman-filtered bus position and flow estimates.

\noindent\textbf{Solves:} per junction per second, which of HOLD, TRANSITION,
or PHASE\_ROTATION maximises immediate corridor bus benefit minus
cross-street cost from the filtered state.  Myopic (no lookahead) and
unlearned: the same state always decides the same way.

\paragraph{Objective mapping (Type~D, not Type~A).} Centralised commits by its
own rule cascade (Alg.~\ref{alg:centralised}), not by the $Z_1$ layer: a myopic
per-second $Z_1$ approximation whose only exact-program quantity is the $Z_4$
veto (Fig.~\ref{fig:objectives}, rule-commit column).
The action space per intersection ($\approx$20 candidates per detection cycle) is:
\begin{center}
\small
\begin{tabular}{@{}p{3.1cm}p{2.6cm}p{2.4cm}p{8.6cm}@{}}
