\noindent\textbf{MILP criterion (primary comparison basis): one scalar
(\cref{tab:objective_terms,eq:opt_crit}).}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item $Z_1$ --- total weighted passenger delay (pax\,s), main + side, bus + car
        (Eq.\,\ref{eq:Z1}); the one objective, always minimised, lower is better
  \item $Z_2$ --- flow-weighted green-wave bandwidth (steps) (Eq.\,\ref{eq:Z2});
        higher is better; an addable linear term at a fixed coefficient
        (estimated from natural-green arrival statistics
        when the online offset signal is not available; see \cref{sec:res_wobj})
  \item $Z_3$ --- accumulated positive schedule deviation (bus arrivals vs.\
        published timetable, $\sigma^+$) (steps)
        (Eq.\,\ref{eq:Z3}); a cap by default, minimised only under the
        disruption-fallback switch
  \item $Z_4$ --- total corridor travel time, buses + general traffic (veh\,h)
        (Eq.\,\ref{eq:Z4}); a cap, never minimised
\end{itemize}

\noindent\textbf{Network KPIs (contextual interpretation):}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
  \item Average bus/car passenger delay (s/pax)
  \item Total passenger delay (pax\,hrs): main-corridor split and side-street split
  \item Total vehicles in system: $N_{\mathrm{car}} + N_{\mathrm{bus}}$
        (demand-starvation check: a reduction signals fewer served passengers, not a
        genuine delay improvement)
  \item Grant rate: fraction of bus detections with TSP $\neq$ NO\_ACTION
  \item Network speed (km/h), throughput, TSP action counts (GE, INS, NO\_ACTION)
\end{itemize}

