\section{Appendix: Mathematical Program at a Glance}
\label{sec:appendix_program}
% ==============================================================================

\cref{sec:milp} spreads the exact program over many pages.  This
appendix compresses it to three questions: what is given, what is
chosen, and what constrains the choice.  Nothing here is new mathematics;
every row points to its defining equation.

\paragraph{What is being solved, in one paragraph.}
Choose, for every intersection and every integer second, which gate is open
($x$), which TSP event forces it ($y$/$s$), where each clock sits ($\phi$),
and when each bus arrives ($\tau$, vacuous if none)--so that the single
scalar of \cref{eq:opt_crit} is minimised.  The criterion is total passenger
delay (\cref{tab:objective_terms}); progression is an addable linear term, and
lateness and corridor travel time are caps. It
returns a Gantt schedule
(Fig.~\ref{fig:sched}): operations per step, optimal offsets, POG-guarded progression, and bus
trajectories steered back onto the timetable (or a car-only plan when $\Bsp = \emptyset$).  Data in, schedule out:

\begin{center}
\small
\begin{tabular}{p{4.9cm}p{5.2cm}p{4.9cm}}
\hline
\textbf{Given (parameters)} & \textbf{Chosen (decisions)} & \textbf{Returned (artefact)} \\
\hline
Arrivals $A$, timetable $\bar{\tau}$, saturation $\mu$, baseline $\bar{x}$, cycles/offsets $C_i,\phi^{\text{init}}$, storage $K_{ij}$, arrival slopes $a^{\sigma},b^{\sigma}$, main-platoon $q^{\text{main}}$, timing/Purdue caps $P^{\text{max}}/T^{\text{minActive}}/H^{\text{hold}}/T^{\text{mon}}/G^{\text{mon}}_{\min}$ &
Operations $x_{i,p,t}$, events $y_{i,k,t}$/$s_{i,k,t}$, offsets $\phi_{i,t}$, POG $\pi^{\text{POG}}_{i,t}$/loss $L^{\text{prog}}_{i,t}$, triggers $e^{\text{trig}}_{i,t}$/$b^{\text{present}}_{i,t}$, bus clocks $\tau_{b,i}$ (if any) &
Per-step gate plan $+$ optimal offsets $\phi^*$ $+$ POG-guarded progression $+$ bus arrival plan (or car-only plan); re-solved from $\hat{X}_{t_c}$ as corrections (\cref{eq:reopt}) \\
\hline
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

